# The formatting commands in Markdown mode put Markdown into the text.

== Ctrl+B wraps the selection in bold markers
modes: markdown
text: one two three
caret: select "two"
keys: ^b
text-is: one **two** three
typing-works

== Ctrl+B again takes the bold markers off
modes: markdown
text: one two three
caret: select "two"
keys: ^b
keys: ^b
text-is: one two three

== Ctrl+I wraps the selection in italic markers
modes: markdown
text: one two three
caret: select "two"
keys: ^i
text-is: one *two* three

== Ctrl+Alt+2 makes the line a level 2 heading
modes: markdown
text: one two three
caret: after "one"
keys: ^%2
text-is: ## one two three
typing-works

== Ctrl+Alt+0 takes the heading off
modes: markdown
text: ## one two three
caret: after "one"
keys: ^%0
text-is: one two three

== Ctrl+Shift+9 quotes the line
modes: markdown
text: one two three
caret: after "one"
keys: ^+9
text-is: > one two three

== Ctrl+Shift+L makes the line a bullet
modes: markdown
text: one two three
caret: after "one"
keys: ^+l
text-is: - one two three

== Ctrl+Shift+N makes the line a numbered item
modes: markdown
text: one two three
caret: after "one"
keys: ^+n
text-is: 1. one two three

== Tab on a list line indents it and Shift+Tab takes the indent off
modes: markdown
text: - one
caret: end
keys: {TAB}
text-is: "  - one"
focus-is: Message body
keys: +{TAB}
text-is: - one
focus-is: Message body
typing-works

== Ctrl+K puts in a link
modes: markdown
text: See
caret: end
type: " "
keys: ^k
wait: 1.5
front-is: Insert Link
type: https://example.com/page
keys: {TAB}
type: the site
keys: {ENTER}
wait: 1
front-is: New Message
text-is: See [the site](https://example.com/page)
typing-works

== Escape in Insert Link changes nothing and returns to the body
modes: markdown
text: See
caret: end
keys: ^k
wait: 1.5
front-is: Insert Link
keys: {ESC}
wait: 1
front-is: New Message
text-is: See
typing-works
